amp(2.5rem,1.5rem+3vw,4.5rem)]"} data-anim={"fade-up"} data-anim-delay={"160"}><p className={"eyebrow m-0 text-white"}>{"This Post"}</p><dl className={"custom-project-specs m-0"}><div><dt>{"Written by"}</dt><dd>{"Rachel Moore"}</dd></div><div><dt>{"Published"}</dt><dd>{"Oct 8, 2026"}</dd></div><div><dt>{"Topic"}</dt><dd>{"Planning"}</dd></div><div><dt>{"Reading time"}</dt><dd>{"7 minutes"}</dd></div></dl></div></aside></section><section id={"cn-ar-body"} className={"custom-section"} aria-label={"The article"}><div className={"container grid gap-x-20 gap-y-14 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_18rem]"}><article className={"custom-article max-w-[44rem]"}><p className={"custom-article-lead"}>{"Two estimates for the same kitchen can be $20,000 apart and both be honest. The difference is almost always in what each one leaves out. After writing about four hundred of them a year, here is what I would look for in anyone's estimate, including ours."}</p><h2 id={"cn-ar-1"}>{"1. A scope you could hand to another builder"}</h2><p>{"Every room, every wall that moves, every fixture that is replaced or kept. If the scope fits on one page, the price is a guess. Ours run from eight to twenty pages for a renovation."}</p><h2 id={"cn-ar-2"}>{"2. Allowances with names and numbers"}</h2><p>{"Tile, lighting, plumbing fixtures and appliances are usually chosen later. A good estimate names each one with its amount: "}<em>{"primary bath tile, $4,200 installed"}</em>{". A low allowance is the easiest way to make an estimate look cheap."}</p><figure><img src={"https://draftmango.com/draftmango/assets/media/placeholder/2560x1440.svg"} alt={"A homeowner and a Draftmango project manager choosing between oak flooring, tile, brick and brass samples on a long wooden table"} width={"2560"} height={"1440"} loading={"lazy"} decoding={"async"} /><figcaption>{"Selections at the Columbia Avenue office: each sample is checked against its allowance before it is ordered."}</figcaption></figure><h2 id={"cn-ar-3"}>{